# Build context for `docker build -f daemon/Dockerfile .` and
# `docker build -f dashboard/Dockerfile .` (both use the repository root, so
# each image can copy the root LICENSE/NOTICE/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md files).
#
# S1: the documented dev run writes credential/PII files inside the tree —
# daemon/data/state.json (account usernames, device identities, audit) and
# daemon/data/secrets.json (sealed passwords) — plus the emulator's
# config.json (which holds a password). None of them may reach the build
# stage or a remote builder cache.
#
# daemon/ and emulator/ stay included: daemon/go.mod replaces ajsproxy with
# ../emulator, so the accountd build needs both module trees.

# S1: a filled deploy/.env holds AJS_MASTER_KEY (the AES-256 key for every
# account password) and the panel admin token; it must never enter the build
# stage or a remote builder cache. The example file is inert and stays, so
# `docker compose config` and the documented copy step keep working.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# AJS-276: the optional HTTPS admin pair lives in deploy/certs (bind-mounted at
# runtime, never built in). A private key must not reach the build stage or a
# remote builder cache.
deploy/certs/

**/data/
**/state.json
**/secrets.json
**/config.json

# Reports, scratch material and lab captures are never part of an image.
research/
results.tsv
docs/
scripts/
.github/
.autoresearch/
autoresearch.json
PLAN.md

# Node build output and dependencies.
**/node_modules/
**/dashboard/dist/
**/dashboard/dist*/
**/dashboard/coverage/

# Local git and editor scratch.
.git/
.gitignore
*.swp
*~

# Binary/vendor payloads and captures.
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.dmp
*.log
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.7z
*.bin
*.exe
*.dll
*.sys
*.cat
